# Writer 11 (tally 2.1, 2.1-8, R-17). L §5.7 A kind test narrows: "A movement or thing variable v bound over a kind P
# is narrowed to a subkind K of P where a written test says it is in K: in a rule whose when is v in K, or a conjunction
# with that test (when v in K and ...), throughout its value and its when; and in if c then e1 else e2 whose condition c
# is v in K or such a conjunction, throughout c and e1. There v's legs and attributes of K are readable."
# "A conjunct that reads them is evaluated only where the test holds, and the conjunction is false where it doesn't":
# the conjunct m.heir == p comes first in the text, and on pay (no heir) the conjunction is false, so community applies.
# Values as L5_7_narrow_when.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons: parties
kind inheritances: transfers
  attr heir: key persons
kind gifts: transfers
  attr giver: key persons
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input inh_day: date
input pay_day: date
input amt: money PLN
move inh: inheritances
  on inh_day
  attr heir = tomek
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt
move pay: transfers
  on pay_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt
def share[m in transfers, p in parties]: num at m.day
  rule community = if p == ania then 1 else 0
  rule inherited beats community = 1 when m.heir == p and m in inheritances
  rule not_heir beats community = 0 when m in inheritances and m.heir != p
ask q: share[inh, ania], share[inh, tomek], share[pay, ania], share[pay, tomek]

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1980-01-01..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1981-01-01..
  inh_day = 2026-03-02
  pay_day = 2026-03-03
  amt = 100.00 PLN
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
=== expect
q: (0, 1, 1, 0)
  cut 2026-01-01
